abstract: "R7 proves a uniform avoidance-profile compiler and preservation theorem for arbitrary finite separation alphabets and arities within the BPZ framework, with exact graph/set/count semantics, finite well-founded DAG closure, alphabet cardinality, and certified pruning. It adds no numerical C11 bound; R6 retains the lower bound 5.295515544509239. AI co-developed with OpenAI's Astra 6 Pro and Codex GPT-6 Astra Extra-High. R7 is Lean checked with only standard Lean axioms; the earlier numerical releases retain their disclosed native-evaluation dependencies."
